id: pm-t1p1jv
title: Model session-suppressed row references in public SDK result types
description: "The existing session mapper replaces declared rows with {id,context_ref} when their facts were already served. PmReadOutputResult<Result> and PmReadOutputResultFor still retain the original row types after budget-omission narrowing. Context focus rows and nested search hits can therefore promise fields that the runtime reference intentionally omits. Existing read-output-contracts unit acceptance proves replacement; this is separate from producer after-cursor metadata optionality in pm-oybmsd."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: output-sessions,sdk,types
created_at: "2026-10-21T04:50:19.034Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T09:35:16.656Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T09:31:00.916Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T09:31:00.916Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Public result declarations model session reference rows at their declared row paths; callers can narrow a reference before accessing original prose or nested hit fields; ordinary non-session rows retain their useful types; independent source and packed declaration consumers fail before and pass after correction while runtime consent suppression budgets and cursors remain unchanged
parent: pm-srns
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: SDK session-capable results admit reference rows at declared paths; ordinary no-session rows stay precise; public reference guard and migration guidance are exported with snapshot acknowledgement.
expected_result: Typed session consumers distinguish delivered facts from previously served references without unsafe casts.
actual_result: "Source typecheck and packed declaration consumers pass for context, nested search hits, literal and dynamic maps, optional and overlapping paths and numeric array segments. Node/Bun packed matrices pass; unchanged declarations fail the regression consumer."
